WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Night falls at a gurdwara.

2
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.740
A large book is carried on a
Sikh's head to a room of its own.

3
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:11.160
At dawn it returns to a
raised throne, under a canopy.

4
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.270
A whisk is waved over it.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.740
It has 1,430 pages.

6
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.340
Sikhs call it their living Guru.

7
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.970
So how can a book be a living teacher?

8
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.120
And with no priests, who leads?

9
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.240
In this mission, you'll trace how a
book of hymns became the Guru in 1708,

10
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.140
and how Sikhs use it.

11
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:37.400
Then you'll see who leads Sikhs today,
and meet a water-carrier on a battlefield.

12
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:41.270
Your mission: explain how a
book can be a living teacher,

13
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.650
and who leads when there are no priests.
